      <font color="#0066FF">Q13:</font>What are different types of access modifiers?</strong> <br>



        <font color="#0066FF">



        <strong>Ans</strong>: </font>There are following four types of access modifiers <strong><br>



      <font color="#0066FF">public:</font></strong> Any thing declared as public can be accessed from anywhere. <br>



      <font color="#0066FF">



<strong>private:</strong></font> Any thing declared as private can&rsquo;t be seen outside of its class.<br>



      <font color="#0066FF">



<strong>protected:</strong></font> Any thing declared as protected can be accessed by classes in the same package and subclasses in the other packages.<br>



      <font color="#0066FF">



<strong>default modifier :</strong></font> Can be accessed only to classes in the same package.</font></P>



      <P align="left" class="style3" dir="ltr"><font face="Verdana" size="2"><b>
